@using RouteBaseWeb.Services.Tracks
@model VersionHistoryPanel
@* Version history — owner only, so the caller gates it. History is not a public fact about a ride: a friend
   viewing it has no business reading what it looked like before you cropped it (the API enforces this too).

   This is the ONE place a ride's version changes (EditorSurfaces): restore a version · undo the save that
   wrote one · reset to original. There is deliberately no second door — a head cannot move while the ride is
   checked out, so the editor cannot host one.

   `data-checked-out` is that fact, server-rendered from the ride's own checkout pointer: while it is set,
   every action here is refused by the server, so the panel says so up front instead of firing a 409.

   `data-version-count` / `data-any-commit` let the panel decide whether to fetch the list AT ALL. Most rides
   are imported once and never edited, and the panel used to spend an HTTP round-trip on every owner page load
   just to learn it had nothing to show. They are raw counts, NOT a verdict — the rule lives in hasHistory()
   (version-history-model.ts), once.

   Every id below is a DOM contract read by version-history.ts. *@

<div class="det-custom-panel" id="versionHistoryPanel"
     data-track-id="@Model.TrackId"
     data-lifecycle="@Model.Lifecycle"
     data-checked-out="@(Model.CheckedOut ? "true" : "false")"
     data-version-count="@Model.Facts.VersionCount"
     data-any-commit="@(Model.Facts.AnyCommit ? "true" : "false")">
    <div class="det-custom-header">
        <i class="bi bi-clock-history"></i> Version history
        <button type="button" class="btn-cockpit btn-cockpit-ghost btn-cockpit-sm ms-auto"
                id="parkToggleBtn" hidden></button>
    </div>
    <div class="det-custom-body">
        @* Only while the ride is checked out. The panel's actions are inert until the edit is resolved, and
           saying which edit is holding it is the difference between a dead button and a next step. *@
        <div class="det-notice det-notice--warn" id="versionCheckedOutNotice" hidden>
            This ride has an edit open. Resume or discard it (top of the page) to change versions.
        </div>
        <ul class="version-list" id="versionList"></ul>
        <div class="det-notice det-notice--info" id="versionStatus">Loading&hellip;</div>
        <div class="version-panel-actions" id="versionPanelActions" hidden>
            <button type="button" class="btn-cockpit btn-cockpit-danger btn-cockpit-sm" id="versionResetBtn">
                Reset track to original&hellip;
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
